# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted. Git guesses "binary" by looking for a
# NUL byte near the start of a file, and some PDF generators (ReportLab) emit none — so
# public/docs/aspirova-technical-overview.pdf was classified as LF text and a checkout on a
# machine with core.autocrlf=true rewrote it with CRLF, growing it 46,054 -> 46,451 bytes and
# corrupting it. Declare the types explicitly rather than relying on the heuristic.

*.pdf   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
